{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "AH1806-W-7",
 "kind": "sensor",
 "manufacturer": "Diodes Incorporated",
 "title": "AH1806: micropower omnipolar Hall-effect switch with open-drain output",
 "source": {
  "document": "DS36104",
  "revision": "Rev. 8 - 2, February 2018",
  "pages": 12
 },
 "summary": "A Hall-effect switch that responds to either magnetic pole: its open-drain output pulls low once the field through the package face, north or south, passes about 30 G, and lets go when the field drops back below about 20 G. It wakes for 75 µs out of every 75 ms to sample the field, so it averages 8 µA (24 µW) at 3 V; between samples the output holds its latched state. Two chopper-stabilised Hall plates feed the comparators. It runs from 2.5 to 5.5 V over -40 to 85 °C. AH1806-W-7 is the SC59 part on a 3000-piece 7-inch reel.",
