  {
   "id": "typical",
   "title": "Typical application",
   "page": 2,
   "description": "The switch runs from a 2.5 V to 5.5 V rail on VDD with a ceramic capacitor CIN from VDD to ground beside it to steady the supply and help reject noise. A pull-up RL from VDD to the open-drain OUTPUT gives a logic-level signal that is high with no field and low while a magnet of either pole is near.",
