 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Omnipolar switching",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Field is counted positive for a south pole facing the marked side and negative for a north pole. With no field the output is off and pulled up to VOH. When the field rises past Bops (south) or below Bopn (north) the output turns on and sits at VOL; it turns off again once the field returns inside Brps or Brpn. Each pole has its own hysteresis band of Bhy between operate and release points."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Sleep and sample cycle",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "An internal timer powers the Hall front end for tAWAKE (75 µs typ) once every tPERIOD (75 ms typ), a 0.1 % duty cycle. During that window the part draws IDD(awake), about 3 mA; for the rest of the period it sleeps at IDD(sleep), about 5 µA, so the average is IDD(avg), 8 µA typ at 3 V. At the end of each awake window the field is sampled and the result latched onto the output, which holds until the next sample."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power-up",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "VDD must already be within 2.5 V to 5.5 V at power-up for sampling to be guaranteed. The output can be relied on from the second sample onward, about 150 ms after power is applied."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Internal arrangement",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Two Hall plates each feed an offset-cancellation stage, an amplifier, a comparator with hysteresis and a latch. An output driver controller combines the two latches and drives an NMOS whose drain is OUTPUT and source GND. A sleep/awake logic block switches power to the front end. The chopper-stabilised design gives low switch-point drift with temperature and better tolerance of package stress."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Choosing CIN and RL",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Recommended values: CIN, 10 nF to 100 nF from VDD to GND, for a stable supply and better noise immunity; RL, 10 kΩ to 100 kΩ, as the pull-up on the open-drain output."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Hall element position",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "SC59: the element sits 0.7 to 0.9 mm in from the long body edge opposite pins 1 and 2, 1.3 to 1.5 mm from the short body edge on the pin 2 side, and 0.10 to 0.20 mm below the marked top face. SOT553: 0.75 to 0.85 mm from the pin 1 end of the body, 0.45 to 0.67 mm in from the long edge on the pin 4 and 5 side, and 0.22 to 0.38 mm below the marked face. SIP-3, both lead forms: 1.90 to 2.10 mm from the pin 3 side of the body, 1.6 to 1.8 mm below the top edge, and 0.27 to 0.48 mm behind the marked face; the lead centre is 0.63 to 0.84 mm behind that face."
  }
 ],
